## Overfitting and Underfitting
A critical challenge in machine learning is balancing the model's complexity so it performs well on both the training data and new, unseen test data.
*   **Overfitting:** Occurs when a model learns the training data *too* well, including its noise and outliers. It has high variance and low bias. The model performs exceptionally on training data but fails to generalize to test data.
    *   *Solutions:* Collect more data, simplify the model (fewer features/parameters), or use regularization techniques (like L1/L2 penalty).
*   **Underfitting:** Occurs when a model is too simple to capture the underlying structure of the data. It has low variance and high bias. The model performs poorly on both training and testing datasets.
    *   *Solutions:* Use a more complex model, engineer better features, or train the model longer.
